{
  "_why": "Role track for HEAT TREATMENT, a new trade (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #8, sheet 17). fam_heat_treatment binds four NCO codes at job-domain specificity 50: 8121.3701 'Heat Treating Furnace Operator', 8121.4800 'Hardener, Metal', 8121.4900 'Temperer, Metal' and 8121.4700 'Annealer, Metal'. Every other 8121 code stays on fam_metal_processing.",
  "_scope": "THE HEAT-TREATMENT SHOP, NOT THE MELT SHOP. A foundryman who melts metal in an induction furnace is the Foundry / Forging trade (sheet 19); this trade hardens, tempers, carburises, nitrides and anneals finished or machined parts, in a job shop or a captive HT line.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS heat_experience, asked FIRST. Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm; Medium adds 2 (process, furnace); Advanced adds 2 (testing, material). Worst case 2 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 7 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 17 (a new trade, no ratified page). Section title 'Heat treatment, processes & capability'. Its rows are Processes, Equipment (furnaces), Testing and Materials, and every row has exactly one question here.",
  "pack_id": "qp_heat_treatment",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_heat_treatment",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v1 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #8): new trade. Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-17 level ladder (Trainee/Operator/Skilled/Senior/Supervisor, mandatory); 1 separating confirm, the sheet's question verbatim, asked of skilled AND senior (the owner's standing rule: the sheet writes none for senior); supervisor by rule. Medium Q6 process, Q7 furnace; Advanced Q9 testing, Q10 material, gated years OR rung. Deviations recorded: Q11 'shift/site' is the shared qp_universal shift question and Q12 the shared ITI block (no per-trade row; 3D / PLC / EDM precedent for a new trade); no fresher items. Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
